<Layout title="Verify your immigration representative"><PageHero eyebrow="MAKE INFORMED CHOICES" title="Know who you are working with." text="Take time to verify your representative before sharing sensitive documents or paying for advice."/><article class="container prose"><h2>Use the official register</h2><p>The College of Immigration and Citizenship Consultants maintains a public register. Search for your consultant by name or College ID, and review the current licence, eligibility, contact details and any relevant disciplinary information.</p><p>Verto’s stated immigration contact is {site.consultant}, College ID {site.collegeId}. Use the register to check the current record and confirm the contact details directly.</p><p><a href={site.register} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open the College’s public register ↗</a></p><h2>Check the contact details</h2><p>A familiar name or licence number by itself is not enough. Compare the company, telephone and email information with the official record and contact the licensee through a verified channel if anything is unclear.</p><h2>Understand the agreement</h2><p>Ask for a written agreement describing the work, fees, cancellation terms and the person providing the service. Clarify the payment recipient and any different merchant name before paying.</p><h2>Expect honest limitations</h2><p>No representative can guarantee an approval or control a government processing date. Be cautious about promises of guaranteed visas or jobs.</p><p>Source: <a href="https://register.college-ic.ca/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">College public register and verification guidance</a>. Always check the current official record.</p></article></Layout>
